# The `ns_kind="triton"` hook — the fused Triton Newton–Schulz arm's wiring.
#
# WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT AN EDIT: at 2026-10-17 a concurrent lane holds
# `port/src/dormouse/train/optim.py` and `port/src/dormouse/config.py` dirty
# (the NorMuon/SF rework, 257 lines in optim.py), and the lane brief forbids
# editing files another agent is in. The new code this hook calls is committed
# separately and is inert until this patch lands:
#
#   port/src/dormouse/train/ns_kernels.py   (the fused chain + its COUNTED fallback)
#   port/tests/test_ns_triton.py            (the gates; 3 of them are skipif'd on
#                                            `"triton" in optim.NS_KINDS` and run
#                                            the moment this patch is applied)
#   port/scripts/bench_ns_triton.py         (the bench)
#
# APPLY (from the repo root):   git apply port/ns_triton_hook.patch
# It applies cleanly to the working tree as of 2026-10-17 (HEAD 6fda506 + that
# lane's edits) — `git apply --check` was run against exactly that tree.
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#   optim.py     NS_KINDS += "triton"; the LOUD refusal names it; `zeropower_via_ns`
#                gains a keyword-only `counters` and the triton arm (one lazy
#                import + one call into ns_kernels); `Muon.counters`; the arm's
#                counters forwarded in `_orthogonalize` ONLY for `triton`, so the
#                `classic`/`gram` call shapes stay exactly what every pin and spy
#                in this tree was written against; `MixOptimizer.counters`.
#   config.py    NS_KINDS += "triton" + the field and refusal docstrings.
#   loop.py      merge + clear `opt.counters` after `opt.step()`, so `ns_triton` /
#                `ns_triton_fallback` + the reason reach the log line (ADR-0019).
#   tests/test_muon_fast.py
#                `@pytest.mark.parametrize("kind", optim.NS_KINDS)` gates every arm
#                on the bf16 rung, so the new arm is picked up automatically — and
#                it needs a `Counters()` to record its fallback (ADR-0019). Three
#                call sites get one. That gate is what caught the fallback dropping
#                `ns_dtype` while this arm was being written.
#
# NOT in this patch, deliberately: `ns_kind` stays `classic` by default and no
# preset changes, so this is an opt-in arm with no effect until a config names it.
